{
  "summary": "Enforces strict input buffer parsing in libbitcoinkernel's object creation functions. `btck_transaction_create` and `btck_block_create` are updated to return null if unconsumed trailing bytes remain in the provided buffer after deserializing a transaction or block. Header documentation and kernel tests are updated accordingly.",
  "problem": "Callers passing serialized transaction or block buffers with excess trailing bytes to `btck_transaction_create` or `btck_block_create` currently succeed silently, leaving the deserialized object's byte length out of sync with the input buffer length.",
  "evidence": [
    "Commit message and PR description: \"`btck_transaction_create` and `btck_block_create` ignore any bytes after the serialized object, so the object's serialized length does not match the buffer.\"",
    "Author description: \"Two new checks in `test_kernel` append one byte to a valid transaction and to a valid block. They fail on master and pass with the change.\""
  ],
